IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `fa-2006-maternity`

-- A New Tax System (Family Assistance) Act 1999 as in force on 30 August 2006 (C2006C00402) -- the 1 July 2006 substitution of
-- the FTB rates under Schedule 4, computed from the formulas in ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A00490.2006-07-01.formulas.md,
-- beside fa-2006-maternity.l4 (unchanged).
--
-- fa-2006-maternity.l4 takes the 2006-07 FTB amounts as inputs (`Rates in 2006`), because the compilation prints only the
-- statutory figures and Schedule 4 substitutes new ones every 1 July (REQ-0063). The sidecar gives the two formulas the text lost:
--   * Sch 4 cl 5(1): indexation factor = Index number for most recent reference quarter / Index number for base quarter, to 3
--     decimal places, raised by 0.001 where the 4th place is greater than 4 (cl 5(2)), never below 1 (cl 5(3));
--   * Sch 4 cl 7(1): CPC rate x 16.6%, substituted for the FTB under 13 child rate where it exceeds the rate as indexed (cl 7(2)),
--     raised to the next multiple of $3.65 (cl 7(5)).
-- From the text: cl 4 (current figure x factor) and cl 6 (rounding to the nearest multiple of the rounding base, a half up); the cl
-- 3 table: every amount used here is indexed on 1 July against a December reference quarter, with rounding base $3.65 (items 1,
-- 8A, 9) or $73.00 (item 12, FTB additional HIFA (A)).
--
-- STILL INPUTS, so REQ-0063 stays open: the current figures immediately before 1 July 2006 (the 2005-06 figures, set by earlier
-- substitutions that no deposited text holds), the CPI index numbers (Australian Statistician), and the CPC rate (s 3(7), whose
-- own formula is image.002.png, not transcribed, and which turns on Social Security Act pension rates). Each amount's base
-- quarter is "the highest December quarter before the reference quarter", taken here to be the same quarter for all of them.
--
-- SEAT and method as fa-2006-maternity.l4. See NOTES.md.

§ `Family Assistance Act as at 2006 -- the 1 July 2006 substitution of the FTB rates`

@export What is the Schedule 4 indexation factor (Sch 4 cl 5, as in 2006)?
GIVEN `index number for most recent reference quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc The CPI index number for the December quarter before the indexation day
      `index number for base quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc The CPI index number for the highest earlier December quarter
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the 2006 indexation factor` MEANS
    IF `raised` LESS THAN 1 THEN 1 ELSE `raised`
    WHERE
        `ratio` MEANS `index number for most recent reference quarter` DIVIDED BY `index number for base quarter`
        `to 3 places` MEANS FLOOR (`ratio` TIMES 1000) DIVIDED BY 1000
        `fourth place` MEANS FLOOR (`ratio` TIMES 10000) MINUS (FLOOR (`ratio` TIMES 1000) TIMES 10)
        `raised` MEANS IF `fourth place` GREATER THAN 4 THEN `to 3 places` PLUS 0.001 ELSE `to 3 places`

@export What is an FTB amount after its 1 July 2006 indexation (Sch 4 cll 4, 6, as in 2006)?
GIVEN `current figure` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount immediately before 1 July 2006
      `factor` IS A NUMBER @desc The indexation factor under cl 5
      `rounding base` IS A NUMBER @desc Column 5 of the cl 3 table for the amount ($3.65, or $73 for the additional HIFA)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the 2006 indexed amount` MEANS
    FLOOR ((`current figure` TIMES `factor` DIVIDED BY `rounding base`) PLUS 0.5) TIMES `rounding base`

-- cl 7(1), (2), (5): the CPC figure, raised to the next multiple of $3.65, replaces the indexed rate only if it exceeds it.
@export What is the FTB under 13 child rate from 1 July 2006 (Sch 4 cll 4, 5, 7, as in 2006)?
GIVEN `rate before 1 July` IS A NUMBER @desc The FTB under 13 child rate immediately before 1 July 2006
      `factor` IS A NUMBER @desc The indexation factor under cl 5
      `CPC rate` IS A NUMBER @desc The CPC rate on 1 July 2006 (s 3(7)), a year
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the FTB under 13 child rate from 1 July 2006` MEANS
    IF `from the CPC rate` GREATER THAN `indexed` THEN `from the CPC rate` ELSE `indexed`
    WHERE
        `indexed` MEANS `the 2006 indexed amount` `rate before 1 July` `factor` 3.65
        `sixteen point six percent` MEANS `CPC rate` TIMES 16.6 DIVIDED BY 100
        `from the CPC rate` MEANS
            IF FLOOR (`sixteen point six percent` DIVIDED BY 3.65) TIMES 3.65 EQUALS `sixteen point six percent`
            THEN `sixteen point six percent`
            ELSE (FLOOR (`sixteen point six percent` DIVIDED BY 3.65) PLUS 1) TIMES 3.65

-- The `Rates in 2006` record for 1 July 2006, from the figures in force immediately before it.
@export What were the FTB amounts from 1 July 2006, from those before it (Sch 4, as in 2006)?
GIVEN `before` IS A `Rates in 2006` @desc The FTB amounts in force immediately before 1 July 2006
      `index number for most recent reference quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc The CPI index number for the December quarter 2005
      `index number for base quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc The CPI index number for the highest earlier December quarter
      `CPC rate` IS A NUMBER @desc The CPC rate on 1 July 2006 (s 3(7)), a year
GIVETH A `Rates in 2006`
`the FTB amounts from 1 July 2006` MEANS
    `Rates in 2006` WITH
        `FTB under 13 child rate (A1)`              IS `the FTB under 13 child rate from 1 July 2006` (`before`'s `FTB under 13 child rate (A1)`) `f` `CPC rate`
        `FTB gross supplement amount (A)`           IS `the 2006 indexed amount` (`before`'s `FTB gross supplement amount (A)`) `f` 3.65
        `FTB additional HIFA (A)`                   IS `the 2006 indexed amount` (`before`'s `FTB additional HIFA (A)`) `f` 73
        `FTB standard rate (B), youngest under 5`   IS `the 2006 indexed amount` (`before`'s `FTB standard rate (B), youngest under 5`) `f` 3.65
        `FTB standard rate (B), youngest 5 or over` IS `the 2006 indexed amount` (`before`'s `FTB standard rate (B), youngest 5 or over`) `f` 3.65
    WHERE
        `f` MEANS `the 2006 indexation factor` `index number for most recent reference quarter` `index number for base quarter`
